From 91ffb0752543475969df993351b3d3e95e6ea2ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:22:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 216/294] gallium/pvr: full VDM vertex state, and the same
 state reproduces a captured draw

Captured the working Vulkan driver's geometry control stream for one draw (PVR_DEBUG=cs, open
kernel driver bound, offscreen vkrender triangle; the decoded dump is in
open-driver-perf/captures/). It settles several things the driver was guessing at:

- A draw stream is PPP state block -> VDM state -> index list -> terminate, where the TA state
  lives in a memory block named by VDMCTRL_PPP_STATE_UPDATE, not inline packets.
- The VDM state carries the whole vertex half: VS data address (STATE2), code address (STATE3),
  output size (STATE4) and allocation sizes (STATE5), all behind vs_data_addr_present +
  vs_other_present. A stream with only the data address runs the attribute fetch and never starts
  a vertex shader.
- Those PDS addresses are offsets within the PDS heap, not general-heap device addresses.
- The captured draw's 5 output dwords are gl_Position + the gl_PointSize write pco adds, matching
  what this driver's VS now allocates.

So: pvr_csb_emit_vdm_state() takes the whole vertex state, computes STATE1..5 from the same
presence flags that set the header bits, and includes a port of the reference's
pvr_arch_calculate_vertex_cam_size() (copied: it is feature-value thresholds, not a rule to
re-derive; a wrong cam_size changes how much vertex data the hardware keeps, silently).

The probe now checks this against the capture instead of against itself: packing the captured
draw's field values must reproduce the captured dwords exactly (4c000f80 00002880 000027c0
00000005 20000441). It does. The probe's own draw stream carries the same STATE0 for its own
values, and the vertex shader reports the captured 5 varying dwords.

Vertex map work that fell out of the same comparison:
- alloc after lowering, not before: pco's lowering adds the gl_PointSize output, so a map built
  from pre-lowering NIR misses it and the translator writes it to register 0;
- ported the reference's ordering (attributes, sysvals, position, generic varyings grouped by
  interpolation mode, then the special slots) instead of the previous position-only map;
- attribute program PDS temps/data sizes are exported for STATE5.

Verification: probe exits 0, ALL PASS under the DRM noop shim; VDM capture conformance passes.
Not yet done, from the same capture: PPP/TA state block assembly, TA PDS bases with a fragment
PDS kick program, the terminate sequence, and moving the attribute program into the PDS heap so
STATE2/3 carry heap offsets. Those are first-draw work.
